
========================================================================================================
drift.py — signed balance drift over decisions already made
measurement only: nothing is tuned, re-decided or re-ranked
========================================================================================================

========================================================================================================
SIGNED BALANCE DRIFT — BenchRec eval
========================================================================================================

  drift  =  (ledger value the controller attached)
            - (ledger value the label names)          per auto-closed row, in cents

  drift > 0   more ledger value attached than the label names
  drift < 0   less
  drift = 0   equal value, which INCLUDES wrong postings onto equal-valued keys

  Amounts are used with the sign the dataset stores. A statement debit is
  positive, a statement credit negative, and a correctly matched ledger row
  carries the same sign as its statement row. Nothing is negated or abs()'d.

  This is mis-ATTRIBUTION, not loss. The statement value is posted either way;
  one account is overstated and another understated. exposure.py reports the
  full value at risk. This reports direction and cancellation.

  auto-closed rows measured        28,915
    key sets agree, drift = 0      28,443   (98.368%)
    key sets differ                472   (1.632%)

  All drift originates in 472 of 28,915 decisions. The rest contribute exactly
  zero and need no amount lookup: an identical key set carries an identical value
  whichever ledger rows it denotes.

  keys per posted answer           {1: 28915}
    Every auto-closed answer is a single key. This is structural, not
    incidental: controller.py escalates whenever set completion adds a key
    (t_add), so a multi-key answer can never reach auto-close.
  label stratum of those rows      {'single-key': 28588, 'multi-key': 293, 'blank': 34}

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMPUTABILITY — where the difference is defined, and where it is not
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  A rows 37,123   distinct allocation keys 22,779
  keys carried by rows of one amount   20,213 (88.735%)
  keys carried by rows of >1 amount    2,566 (11.265%)  <- amount not determined by the data

  of the 472 rows whose key sets differ:
    drift EXACT                        207   (43.856%)
    drift BOUNDED only                 265   (56.144%)
      because a key in the symmetric difference is carried by several
      ledger rows of different amounts and matchId is blank
    no bound at all (key absent from A)  0

    width of those intervals: median 41.18M, max 1.45B
    No interval is collapsed to a point anywhere in this report.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NET AND GROSS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  On the 28,650 rows where drift is exact (207 of them non-zero):

    net   signed drift                -4.01B
    gross absolute drift               4.97B
    net / gross                      80.827%   <- 100% means no cancellation at all
    cancelled                        952.07M

  Adding the 265 bounded rows, the net over ALL 28,915 auto-closed rows lies in:
    [ -11.35B , 6.45B ]
    gross in  [ 10.04B , 25.82B ]

  Read the net as the extent to which automating these decisions moved the
  ledger in one direction rather than washing out. It is not a loss figure.

